<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12742" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-κᾰλύπτω</span></b> , aor. 2
		
			Pass.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-καλύφην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CPR</u>
					1.239.5
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, etc.:—<i>uncover,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν κεφαλήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.119
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ στήθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					352a
				</span></i>
			:—in 
				Pass.
			, of land <i>left</i> cultivable by the Nile (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκάλυφοσ—, ἀρούρας β́
					ἀποκαλυφείσης . . αἰγιαλοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PIand.</u>
					27.12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				27.60
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i/ii A.D.)</span>:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκαλύπτεσθαι τὴν κεφαλήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Crass.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>disclose, reveal,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόδε τῆς διανοίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					352a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴντῆς ῥητορικῆς δύναμιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					455d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				460a
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>reveal one's whole mind,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				55
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				2.880e
			</span></i>:—in 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Ki.</u>
				2.27
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκαλύπτεσθαι πρός τι</span>
			<i>letone's designs</i> upon a thing <i>become known,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				17.62
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.23
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be made known,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Matt.
				10.26
			</span></i>, etc.; of persons, <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Thess.</u>
				2.3
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι ἀποκεκαλυμμένοι</span>
			<i>naked,</i> i.e. <i>shameless,</i> words, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Vit.Hom.</u>
				214
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>unmask,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Cat.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Vit.Auct.</u>
				23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of the
			epiglottis, <i>raise,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>de An.</u>
				422a2
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			).</div>
